    "title": "Lenox pop-up bar at Avaloch opens near Tanglewood this summer - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sarah Darmanjian ,\n11 hours ago\nLENOX, Mass. (WNYT)- A new pop-up bar at Avaloch in Lenox is giving Tanglewood concertgoers a place to stop for drinks before heading to a show.\nThe seasonal bar is open on Avaloch’s front lawn while the hotel, formerly known as the Apple Tree Inn, goes through renovations. Visitors can get beer, wine, cocktails and nonalcoholic drinks before walking to a concert at Tanglewood.\nLawn games are also available, including badminton, cornhole and KanJam. Rotating food trucks are on site as well.\nThe pop-up is open Fridays and Saturdays from 3 to 8 p.m., Sundays from noon to 5 p.m. and select Tuesdays before popular artist concerts at Tanglewood.",
    "summary": "(WNYT)- A new pop-up bar at Avaloch in Lenox is giving Tanglewood concertgoers a place to stop for drinks before heading to a show. The seasonal bar is open on Avaloch’s front lawn while the hotel, formerly known as the Apple Tree Inn, goes through renovations. Visitors can get beer, wine, cocktails and nonalcoholic drinks before walking to a concert at Tanglewood. Lawn games are also available, including badminton, cornhole and KanJam. The pop-up is open Fridays and Saturdays from 3 to 8 p.m., Sundays from noon to 5 p.m. and select Tuesdays before popular artist concerts at Tanglewood.",
